WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.640
Part six: the tax audit. For a client under section 44 A B, SimplyFile works through Form 3 C D with the auditor - whether an audit is needed, what moved since last year, the clauses that apply to this client, and the points still open.

2
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:31.689
Sri Venkateswara Traders, a partnership firm. From the books already mapped in Intake, the turnover is three point two crore - above the one crore limit, so a tax audit is needed.

3
00:00:32.296 --> 00:00:45.376
What the books cannot show, the firm answers. If cash receipts and cash payments are each within five percent, the limit becomes ten crore - and the answer changes at once.

4
00:00:45.984 --> 00:00:55.684
Here they are not, so the audit stays - and the year is marked as a tax audit, which also moves the due date to the thirty first of October.

5
00:00:56.282 --> 00:01:12.652
Every mapped line of the profit and loss account and the balance sheet, this year against last. Last year comes from last year's statements, last year's filed return, or - as here - the previous-year column in this year's accounts.

6
00:01:13.265 --> 00:01:30.495
The lines worth a look are flagged: rent nearly doubled and interest doubled, salaries and travel up sharply, unsecured loans tripled, creditors up two thirds - while sales grew about eight percent. And a donation that was there last year is gone.

7
00:01:31.094 --> 00:01:41.074
One click turns a flag into an audit point. Rent up eighty nine percent - is the new lease on record, and was TDS deducted?

8
00:01:41.688 --> 00:01:45.868
Every line is a search away - say, the loans.

9
00:01:46.469 --> 00:02:05.429
The Form 3 C D checklist - only the clauses that apply to this client. A firm gets clause nine, partners and their shares; rent and interest bring clause twenty one b, payments without TDS; loans bring clause thirty one, loans taken or repaid in cash.

10
00:02:06.032 --> 00:02:10.592
Each clause is marked as it is worked through, with a note.

11
00:02:11.953 --> 00:02:16.873
Marking a clause as an issue opens an audit point by itself.

12
00:02:19.344 --> 00:02:31.244
Audit points: what still needs an answer before the report is signed - from the year-on-year flags, from the checklist, or added by hand, each with the person who answers it.

13
00:02:31.859 --> 00:02:42.279
A tax preparer may raise points; a reviewer, the auditor, a partner or the firm admin clears them - and every point keeps who raised it and when.

14
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:59.190
The tax audit: the limits, the flags, the 3 C D clauses and who may clear a point are all SimplyFile's own rules, kept as chips - change a limit when the law changes, and every client follows. Thank you for watching.
